### Variáveis globais
@base = http://localhost:8000/api
@contentType = application/json

####################################################################
### CDU002 - Auto Cadastro
####################################################################

### 1) Cadastro válido — devolve access + refresh já autenticados
# @name cadastro
POST {{base}}/usuarios/cadastro/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "username": "maria_convivente",
    "email": "maria@example.com",
    "nome": "Maria Silva",
    "password": "SenhaForte!2026",
    "password_confirmacao": "SenhaForte!2026"
}

###

####################################################################
### CDU001 - Fazer Login
####################################################################

### 1) Login válido — devolve access + refresh
# @name login
POST {{base}}/usuarios/login/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "email": "maria@example.com",
    "password": "SenhaForte!2026"
}

###

### 2) Conferir o perfil usando o access token recebido no login
# Copie o valor de "access" da resposta acima para @accessToken
@accessToken = COLE_O_ACCESS_TOKEN_AQUI

GET {{base}}/usuarios/me/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 3) Renovar o access token usando o refresh token recebido no cadastro
### 3) Renovar o access token usando o refresh token recebido no login
POST {{base}}/token/refresh/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "refresh": "COLE_O_REFRESH_TOKEN_AQUI"
}

###

####################################################################
### Fluxo Alternativo I - dados inválidos/faltantes (CDU002)
####################################################################

### 4) Campos obrigatórios faltando — 400 com os campos destacados
POST {{base}}/usuarios/cadastro/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "nome": "Sem usuario, email ou senha"
}

###

### 5) Senha fraca (numérica/comum) — 400 com mensagem em "password"
POST {{base}}/usuarios/cadastro/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "username": "joao_convivente",
    "email": "joao@example.com",
    "nome": "Joao",
    "password": "12345678",
    "password_confirmacao": "12345678"
}

###

### 5b) Confirmação diferente da senha — 400 com "As senhas não coincidem." em "password_confirmacao"
POST {{base}}/usuarios/cadastro/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "username": "joao_convivente",
    "email": "joao@example.com",
    "nome": "Joao",
    "password": "SenhaForte!2026",
    "password_confirmacao": "SenhaForte!2027"
}

###

### 6) Username já cadastrado — 400 com mensagem em "username"
POST {{base}}/usuarios/cadastro/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "username": "maria_convivente",
    "email": "outra@example.com",
    "nome": "Outra Maria",
    "password": "SenhaForte!2026",
    "password_confirmacao": "SenhaForte!2026"
}

###

### 3b) Login válido por username (não documentado no CDU001, adicional p/ frontend já existente)
POST {{base}}/usuarios/login/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "username": "maria_convivente",
    "password": "SenhaForte!2026"
}

###

####################################################################
### Fluxo Alternativo I - credenciais inválidas (CDU001)
####################################################################

### 4) Senha incorreta — 400 com mensagem genérica
POST {{base}}/usuarios/login/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "email": "maria@example.com",
    "password": "senha_errada"
}

###

### 5) E-mail não cadastrado — mesma mensagem genérica (não revela qual falhou)
POST {{base}}/usuarios/login/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "email": "naoexiste@example.com",
    "password": "qualquer123"
}

###

### 6) Nem e-mail nem username informados
POST {{base}}/usuarios/login/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "password": "qualquer123"
}

###

### 7) Senha faltando
POST {{base}}/usuarios/login/
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
    "email": "maria@example.com"
}
